133		/**
134		 * Every Transfer in every status, newest first, or the one status {@code status} names.
135		 *
136		 * <p><b>Every status, which is design decision 19's reading of the requirement rather
137		 * than a liberty taken with it.</b> The task asks for executed transfers, written against
138		 * a synchronous model where a Transfer is either done or never existed. Under the
139		 * asynchronous lifecycle of ADR-0001 a {@code PENDING} Transfer appearing nowhere would
140		 * make the only list screen actively misleading: an operator would believe their Transfer
141		 * had vanished. The filter is what narrows it to settled Transfers for a caller who wants
142		 * that.
143		 *
144		 * <p>A bare array rather than an object wrapping one, and a status typed as the enum
145		 * rather than a string, both on {@code AccountController#listAccounts}'s reasoning: an
146		 * envelope earns its place when there is something to put beside the items, and design
147		 * decision 31 declines pagination. A status this domain has no name for is refused by the
148		 * conversion, and {@code ProblemDocumentAdvice} reports it against {@code status} in the
149		 * shape a rejected body field gets.
150		 */
